{#
| Variable            | Type   | Description                            |
|---------------------|--------|----------------------------------------|
| page                | object |                                        |
| page.title          | string |                                        |
| page.slug           | string |                                        |
| order               | Order  | @see pages/customer/orders/single.twig |
| thank_you           | string |                                        |
| share_message       | string |                                        |
| short_share_message | string |                                        |
#}
{#
  T-6.07 — the post-purchase page. Technique A, and **derived**, for the third
  time this phase and the third distinct reason.

  ITS NAMED ARTBOARD IS A DIFFERENT SCREEN. `Thank You.pdf` shows a breadcrumb
  reading «الطلبات ‹ تقييم الطلب» over «تقييم الطلب #768467» and «شكرًا لمشاركتك
  رأيك! تم حفظ تقييمك بنجاح.» — **it is the rating success confirmation**, which
  belongs to T-6.08. So this page, like `orders/single.twig` before it, has no
  drawing of its own, and it is built in the language the rest of the order area
  now speaks: `.account-panel`, the shell's own breadcrumb row, T-2.05's buttons.
  Following AC-10 and AC-11 rather than asking a third time for the same ruling;
  reversing it is one commit.

  IT DOES NOT EXTEND `layouts.customer`, AND THAT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT. That shell
  guards its content on `user.type == 'user'` and shows a sign-in prompt
  otherwise — correct for an account page, and **fatal here**, because a guest who
  has just paid would be told to log in instead of being told their order went
  through. The shell's *classes* are reused; its *guard* is not.

  WHAT WAS REMOVED, AND IT IS ONE THING. Upstream opens with a full-bleed
  brand-coloured band and an SVG wave. Nothing in this design has a coloured
  banner anywhere — T-5.10 removed the same construction from the loyalty page
  for the same reason. Everything else upstream renders is still here.

  ⚠ THE PAGE WAS INVISIBLE WITHOUT JAVASCRIPT AND THAT IS FIXED. Upstream marks
  the illustration, the title and the reference `opacity-0`, and `thankyou.js`
  adds `slide-in-start` to fade them in. **If that script does not run, a customer
  who has just paid sees an empty page.** The `opacity-0` classes are gone; the
  animation supplies its own starting opacity from its keyframes, so nothing is
  lost when the script does run.
#}
{% extends "layouts.master" %}

{% block content %}
    {% hook 'thank-you:start' %}

    <div class="container">
        <div class="customer-layout">
            <nav class="customer-layout__breadcrumb" aria-label="{{ trans('theme.customer.breadcrumb') }}">
                <salla-breadcrumb></salla-breadcrumb>
            </nav>

            <div class="customer-layout__content">
                {#
                  THE CONFIRMATION. «Order reference clearly presented» is the
                  criterion, and it is presented as a heading-adjacent line with
                  the platform's own copy-to-clipboard control beside it — kept
                  from upstream, because a reference a customer can copy is worth
                  more than one they must transcribe.
                #}
                <section class="account-panel thankyou-panel">
                    <div class="rtl:-scale-x-100">
                        <img src="{{ 'images/delivery-bro.svg' | asset }}"
                             alt=""
                             class="thanks-item thankyou-panel__art"
                             width="160"
                             height="160">
                    </div>

                    <h1 data-testid="store-thankyou-title" class="thanks-item thankyou-panel__title">
                        {{ thank_you_title }}
                    </h1>

                    <p class="thanks-item thankyou-panel__reference">
                        {{ trans('pages.thank_you.order_id') }}
                        <salla-button data-testid="store-thankyou-order-id" class="relative"
                                      onclick="app.copyToClipboard(event)" color="dark" shape="link"
                                      data-content="{{ order.reference_id }}">
                            <span>#{{ order.reference_id }}</span>
                            <i class="copy-icon sicon-swap-stroke pointer-events-none rtl:mr-1 ltr:ml-1"></i>
                        </salla-button>
                    </p>

                    {#
                      «Next actions offered» — two, and both are real. The first
                      is the platform's own `order.show`, which opens the native
                      order screen inside Salla's apps and the web page outside
                      them; the second is the way back into the store, which
                      upstream never offered from here at all.
                    #}
                    <div class="thankyou-panel__actions">
                        {% include 'components.ui.button' with {
                            label:   trans('pages.thank_you.order_details'),
                            icon:    'newspaper',
                            variant: 'primary',
                            class:   'thankyou-panel__action',
                            attrs:   { 'data-testid': 'store-thankyou-order-details-btn', onclick: "salla.order.show({order_id:'" ~ order.id ~ "', url:'" ~ order.url ~ "'})" }
                        } only %}

                        {% include 'components.ui.button' with {
                            label:   trans('common.elements.back_home'),
                            href:    link('/'),
                            variant: 'secondary',
                            class:   'thankyou-panel__action'
                        } only %}
                    </div>

                    {% if order.instructions %}
                        <div class="thankyou-panel__instructions">{{ order.instructions|raw }}</div>
                    {% endif %}

                    {% for message in messages %}
                        <p class="thankyou-panel__message">{{ message }}</p>
                    {% endfor %}

                    {% hook 'thank-you:items.start' %}

                    {% hook 'thank-you:items.end' %}
                </section>

                {#
                  Split-shipment tracking. **This is the component B6 named for
                  order tracking, and this is the page it was written for** — its
                  own doc comment says so, and it renders nothing for
                  single-shipment orders. T-6.05 records why it is not the
                  timeline.
                #}
                <salla-order-shipments class="block empty:hidden"></salla-order-shipments>

                <salla-next-order-coupon data-testid="store-thankyou-coupon"></salla-next-order-coupon>

                {% if order.is_pickable %}
                    <salla-order-branch data-testid="store-thankyou-branch"></salla-order-branch>
                {% endif %}

                {#
                  THE INVOICE. Sent, or resendable — upstream's own branch, kept
                  whole. The form still submits through `salla.form.onSubmit`, so
                  the request, its loading state and its error handling stay the
                  platform's.
                #}
                <section class="account-panel thankyou-block">
                    <span class="account-tile">
                        {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'newspaper-alt' } only %}
                    </span>

                    {% if order.email_sent %}
                        <p class="thankyou-block__label">{{ trans('pages.thank_you.email_sent') }}</p>
                        <b class="thankyou-block__value" dir="ltr">{{ order.customer.email }}</b>
                    {% else %}
                        <p class="thankyou-block__label">{{ trans('pages.thank_you.resend_email') }}</p>

                        <form id="invoice-form" class="thankyou-block__form"
                              onsubmit="return salla.form.onSubmit('order.sendInvoice', event)">
                            {#
                              The input had a placeholder and no label at all —
                              a placeholder is not an accessible name, and it
                              disappears the moment anything is typed. The label
                              is `sr-only` because the sentence above already
                              names the field on screen.
                            #}
                            <label class="sr-only" for="thankyou-invoice-email">
                                {{ trans('pages.thank_you.resend_email') }}
                            </label>
                            <input data-testid="store-thankyou-email-input"
                                   id="thankyou-invoice-email"
                                   type="email"
                                   name="email"
                                   class="form-input"
                                   placeholder="your@email.com"
                                   autocomplete="email"
                                   dir="ltr"
                                   required>

                            <salla-button data-testid="store-thankyou-email-submit" type="submit"
                                          loader-position="center">
                                <span class="btn__text">{{ trans('blocks.comments.submit') }}</span>
                            </salla-button>
                        </form>
                    {% endif %}
                </section>

                {% if store.contacts.mobile or store.contacts.whatsapp %}
                    <section class="account-panel thankyou-block">
                        <span class="account-tile">
                            {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'mail-letter' } only %}
                        </span>

                        <p class="thankyou-block__label">{{ trans('common.titles.support') }}</p>

                        <div class="thankyou-block__contacts">
                            {% if store.contacts.mobile %}
                                <a class="thankyou-block__contact" href="tel:{{ store.contacts.mobile }}">
                                    {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'phone' } only %}
                                    <b class="unicode" dir="ltr">{{ store.contacts.mobile }}</b>
                                </a>
                            {% endif %}

                            {% if store.contacts.whatsapp %}
                                <a class="thankyou-block__contact"
                                   href="https://wa.me/{{ store.contacts.whatsapp|replace({' ': '', '+': '', '-': ''}) }}"
                                   target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                                    {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'whatsapp' } only %}
                                    <b class="unicode" dir="ltr">{{ store.contacts.whatsapp }}</b>
                                </a>
                            {% endif %}
                        </div>
                    </section>
                {% endif %}

                {% hook 'thank-you:end' %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
    <script defer src="{{ 'checkout.js' | asset }}"></script>
{% endblock %}
